<!--
  Managed-code stripping and the work-giver scan.

  WorkGiverRegistry finds every WorkGiver in this assembly by reflection, which is what lets a
  new kind of work join the job scan without editing a file that belongs to everybody. Nothing
  references those types by name, so a stripped player build is entitled to delete them and the
  colony would simply stop mining, with nothing logged. The editor, the tests and the fast-tier
  mirror projects never strip, so the fault could appear only in a player build - the one place
  it is most expensive to find.

  The whole assembly is preserved because the whole assembly is the simulation: there is nothing
  in it that is not used every tick.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="Odyssey.Sim" preserve="all" />
</linker>
